IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- P1-annex-ii: Annex II of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744),
-- "List of criminal offences referred to in Article 5(1), first subparagraph, point (h)(iii)".
-- Annex II is the same in the text as enacted and as amended (the Omnibus did not touch it), so no function takes a date.
-- The list is data that Article 5(1)(h)(iii) points at; it is not gated by Article 113 (fork F-annex-gate: the Article 5 function that uses it is).
-- The dashes of the Annex carry no number; the encoding numbers them 1 to 16 in the order of the text.
-- Result: a BOOLEAN. An offence that is not on the list is FALSE: Article 5(1)(h)(iii) hands the class "offences referred to in Annex II"
-- to this list, so a case outside the list is the text's own no (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F-annex-ii-closed).

§ `Annex II: the sixteen entries`

-- src:1702 | Criminal offences referred to in Article 5(1), first subparagraph, point (h)(iii):
-- src:1703 | — terrorism,
-- src:1704 | — trafficking in human beings,
-- src:1705 | — sexual exploitation of children, and child pornography,
-- src:1706 | — illicit trafficking in narcotic drugs or psychotropic substances,
-- src:1707 | — illicit trafficking in weapons, munitions or explosives,
-- src:1708 | — murder, grievous bodily injury,
-- src:1709 | — illicit trade in human organs or tissue,
-- src:1710 | — illicit trafficking in nuclear or radioactive materials,
-- src:1711 | — kidnapping, illegal restraint or hostage-taking,
-- src:1712 | — crimes within the jurisdiction of the International Criminal Court,
-- src:1713 | — unlawful seizure of aircraft or ships,
-- src:1714 | — rape,
-- src:1715 | — environmental crime,
-- src:1716 | — organised or armed robbery,
-- src:1717 | — sabotage,
-- src:1718 | — participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above.
@ref Annex II, the list of criminal offences (src:1702-1718)
DECLARE `Annex II offence` IS ONE OF
    `Annex II 1 terrorism`
    `Annex II 2 trafficking in human beings`
    `Annex II 3 sexual exploitation of children, and child pornography`
    `Annex II 4 illicit trafficking in narcotic drugs or psychotropic substances`
    `Annex II 5 illicit trafficking in weapons, munitions or explosives`
    `Annex II 6 murder, grievous bodily injury`
    `Annex II 7 illicit trade in human organs or tissue`
    `Annex II 8 illicit trafficking in nuclear or radioactive materials`
    `Annex II 9 kidnapping, illegal restraint or hostage-taking`
    `Annex II 10 crimes within the jurisdiction of the International Criminal Court`
    `Annex II 11 unlawful seizure of aircraft or ships`
    `Annex II 12 rape`
    `Annex II 13 environmental crime`
    `Annex II 14 organised or armed robbery`
    `Annex II 15 sabotage`
    `Annex II 16 participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above`
    `Annex II no listed offence`   -- the case outside the list: an offence that no entry names

-- The wording of an entry, exactly as the Annex has it (without the dash and the closing comma or full stop).
@ref Annex II, the wording of each entry (src:1703-1718)
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Annex II offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Annex II the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `Annex II 1 terrorism` THEN JUST "terrorism"
    WHEN `Annex II 2 trafficking in human beings` THEN JUST "trafficking in human beings"
    WHEN `Annex II 3 sexual exploitation of children, and child pornography` THEN JUST "sexual exploitation of children, and child pornography"
    WHEN `Annex II 4 illicit trafficking in narcotic drugs or psychotropic substances` THEN JUST "illicit trafficking in narcotic drugs or psychotropic substances"
    WHEN `Annex II 5 illicit trafficking in weapons, munitions or explosives` THEN JUST "illicit trafficking in weapons, munitions or explosives"
    WHEN `Annex II 6 murder, grievous bodily injury` THEN JUST "murder, grievous bodily injury"
    WHEN `Annex II 7 illicit trade in human organs or tissue` THEN JUST "illicit trade in human organs or tissue"
    WHEN `Annex II 8 illicit trafficking in nuclear or radioactive materials` THEN JUST "illicit trafficking in nuclear or radioactive materials"
    WHEN `Annex II 9 kidnapping, illegal restraint or hostage-taking` THEN JUST "kidnapping, illegal restraint or hostage-taking"
    WHEN `Annex II 10 crimes within the jurisdiction of the International Criminal Court` THEN JUST "crimes within the jurisdiction of the International Criminal Court"
    WHEN `Annex II 11 unlawful seizure of aircraft or ships` THEN JUST "unlawful seizure of aircraft or ships"
    WHEN `Annex II 12 rape` THEN JUST "rape"
    WHEN `Annex II 13 environmental crime` THEN JUST "environmental crime"
    WHEN `Annex II 14 organised or armed robbery` THEN JUST "organised or armed robbery"
    WHEN `Annex II 15 sabotage` THEN JUST "sabotage"
    WHEN `Annex II 16 participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above` THEN JUST "participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above"
    WHEN `Annex II no listed offence` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Annex has no wording for an offence it does not name

§ `Annex II: is the offence one that Article 5(1)(h)(iii) refers to`

-- Entry 16 is a limited entry: "participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above".
-- The organisation must be involved in an offence of entries 1 to 15; the caller states that fact.
@ref Annex II, the list of criminal offences, entry 16 (src:1718)
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Annex II offence`
      `the criminal organisation is involved in one or more of the offences listed above` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex II the offence is listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `Annex II no listed offence` THEN FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "offences referred to in Annex II" (a class the text hands to this list: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    WHEN `Annex II 16 participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above` THEN
        `the criminal organisation is involved in one or more of the offences listed above`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "participation in a criminal organisation involved in one or more of the offences listed above" (an organisation involved in none of them is not on the list)
    OTHERWISE TRUE
